commit ce6257eb951dddef7f8f8370fc0b285ec1e51f67

C03: the folder-question exemption gets real word boundaries (FILES1443)

FILES1441 measured nothing: the committed AsksForDeclaredFolder pattern carried two literal backspace characters (0x08) where «\b» belonged, because the root's patch script passed the source through a shell heredoc; the exemption never matched and the App kept vetoing the folder question as a machine slot ask.

Baxy.App UserMessagePolicy.AsksForDeclaredFolder: the pattern is «\b(?:carpeta|directorio|folder|directory)\b», written byte by byte with the editor. Verified by reflection on the compiled assembly: with the folder field declared the question «In which folder (Desktop, Documents, Downloads, or another) should the files be counted?» is accepted; with no fields or another field it is still rejected as machine_slot_ask. App recompiled (BUILD1443). Tests not run (owner order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


